# Release Please owns CHANGELOG.md from 1.4.0 onward: it writes the entry, the compare
# link and the heading structure, and it rewrites the file on every release PR. Prettier
# reflows that output, so the two disagree and the release PR fails its own required
# check — with no author able to fix it, because the next regeneration undoes the fix.
# A generator-owned artifact is ignored here rather than formatted.
CHANGELOG.md

# templates/delivery-contract/commitlint.config.mjs carries a {{scopes}} placeholder that
# `install` renders into real JS; until then it is not valid JS and prettier's parser fails on it.
templates/delivery-contract/commitlint.config.mjs
# .husky/commit-msg is a shell script, not JS/JSON/etc — prettier has no parser for it.
templates/delivery-contract/.husky/
